| Protocol Version      | Disable SMB v1; enable SMB v3 (v3.1.1 preferred) | `Computer Configuration → Policies → Administrative Templates → Network → Lanman Server → Configure SMB v1 server` | Disabled (Windows 10 R1709 or newer)       |
| Encryption           | Require SMB encryption; audit unencrypted traffic | `Computer Configuration → Policies → Windows Settings → Security Settings → Local Policies → Security Options → Microsoft network client: Require encryption`<br>`Audit server/client does not support encryption` | Enabled (Require encryption and audit)    |
| Signing & SPN Validation | Enable SMB signing; enforce SPN validation       | `Computer Configuration → Policies → Windows Settings → Security Settings → Local Policies → Security Options → Microsoft network server: Server SPN target name validation level` | Accept if provided or Required (recommended) |

**Summary:**

- Disable SMB v1 to eliminate legacy protocol vulnerabilities.
- Require SMB v3 encryption to protect data in transit.
- Enable SMB signing and enforce SPN validation to prevent relay and spoofing attacks.
- Audit encryption failures on both client and server sides for visibility.

**Relevant CIS Controls:**

- 9.2 – Ensure Only Approved Ports, Protocols and Services Are Running (v7)
- 4.8 – Uninstall or Disable Unnecessary Services (v8)
- 3.10 – Encrypt Sensitive Data in Transit (v8)
